  "question": {
    "text": "If both the roots of the quadratic equation <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> are real and distinct and they lie in the interval <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><mi>m</mi></math> lies in the interval:<br /><br />Note: In the actual JEE paper interval was <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
